Subject: [PATCH] The full suite on the tip of this delivery: two locks of
 R80b's part 6 compare their kept runs with live ones, and the closure map
 moved on main's head; both runs are made again and kept (cld-advisor; after
 C13's follow-ups)

The full suite on a fresh clone of this delivery's tip (main's 204ee91ed with the 82 entries): 17 failed, 8,718 passed,
74 skipped. Ten fail at main's head as well (run there on the same machine). Four are known: three ask that every gate
pass, and the count of landings is past 40; B1426's fails in a fresh clone at main's head. Three were this seat's:

ONE AND TWO (mended here). R80b's part 6, patches 21 and 22, made B1867's and B1873's locks compare the kept run of
their scripts with a live run, line by line; B1867's lock says what that costs: "when the map changes, the script is
run again and its output kept, as main did." The map moved on main's head (288 nodes to 285; debts joined to nothing 79
to 77, as main closed P-321 and P-747), so each lock found two lines that differ (B1867: lines 1 and 2; B1873: lines 1
and 11, the eleventh the same count). Both scripts are run again and their output kept:
  - B1867 verification/line_or_loop_run.txt: the map's counts (288 nodes, 286 edges to 285, 285; bears-on 4 to 3);
  - B1873 verification/read_checks_run.txt: lines 1 and 7 (93, 16, 77); line 6, which ends in what another script
    prints on failure and which the lock compares only up to its colon, now carries this machine's words.
The arcs' tests: 10 passed. Nothing else changes; the pages that quote the counts of their day keep them.

THREE (mended in place, C14's patch 7): its test named B1294 while checking the archived page, and the paper's
verification manifest counts every test that names a record it lists, so the manifest was stale. The test checks the
archived sentence without the arc's name; the paper's lock passes.

0 of 19.
